==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|setja}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*satjaną}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsɛːtja/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːtja|lang=is}}
* {{a|colloquial}} {{IPA|/ˈsɛːta/|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|setti|sett}}

# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[put]], to [[place]] something somewhere{{jump|is|put|s}}
#: ''Nennirðu að '''setja''' forritunarbókina mína á borðið?''
#:: Could '''put''' my programming book on the table?
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|governs the accusative, dative}} to [[fix]] (something for somebody), to [[determine]] (something regarding somebody), to [[decide]] (something for somebody){{jump|is|determine|s}}
#: ''Hann '''setti''' sér það markmið að grennast.''
#:: He was '''determined''' to lose weight.
#: ''Við '''settum''' okkur að leysa öll dæmin fyrir prófið.''
#:: We '''decided''' to solve all the problems before the examination.
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative|formal}} to formally [[open]]{{jump|is|formally open|s}}
#: ''Að [[setja fund|'''setja''' fund]].''
#:: To '''open''' a meeting.
# {{lb|is|ditransitive|governs the accusative, dative}} (for someone) to [[suppose]] (something){{jump|is|suppose|s}}
# {{lb|is|transitive|governs the accusative}} to [[typeset]]{{jump|is|typeset|s}}
# {{lb|is|impersonal}} used in set phrases
#: ''Eigum við ekki að [[sjá hvað setur|sjá hvað '''setur''']]?''
#:: How about we see what happens?
#: ''Mig [[setja hljóðan|'''setti''' hljóða]] eftir símtalið.''
#:: I couldn't speak after the phone call.
#: ''Það [[setja að|sótti að mér]] kulda.''
#:: I felt cold.
#: ''Þegar hann minntist látinnar konu sinnar [[setja að grát|'''setti''' að]] honum ákafan [[setja að grát|grát]].''
#:: He began crying immensely upon remembering his deceased wife.

